    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement by a Wizard)</em></p><p>A shriveled tongue is pinned to the front cover of this book. Five of these tomes exist, and no one knows which is the original. The tongue on the first <em>Tome of the Stilled Tongue</em> belonged to a treacherous former servant of the lich Vecna; the tongues on the four copies came from other spellcasters who crossed Vecna. The first few pages of each tome are covered in indecipherable scrawls, and the rest are blank.</p><p>While attuned to this item, you can use it as a spellbook and as an @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.equipment24.Item.phbagArcaneFocus]{Arcane Focus}. In addition, while holding the tome, you can take a Bonus Action to cast a spell written in it without expending a spell slot or using any Verbal or Somatic components. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>Only you can remove the tongue from the book’s cover. If you do, all the spells written in the book are erased forever.</p><p>Vecna watches anyone who uses this tome and can write cryptic messages in it, which usually fade once they have been read.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-EMMjceGQOf8xoMDx\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Stilled Tongue</em> compte l’utilisation du jour : lancez le sort choisi sans emplacement depuis vos sorts.</p></section>",
